  "question": {
    "text": "A transparent cube of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>d</mi></math>, made of a material of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>, is immersed in a liquid of refractive index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mo>(</mo><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><msub><mi>μ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>)</mo></math>. A ray is incident on the face <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math> at an angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math> (shown in the figure). Total internal reflection takes place at the point <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">E</mi></math> on the face <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mo>.</mo></math><br />\r<br />\r<img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0055_ffe7b229f3ca.jpg\" style=\"width: 160px; height: 143px;\" /><br />\r<br />\rThen,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>θ</mi></math> must satisfy"
